(1. Purpose and Scope) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 742 Td
(This handbook provides a clear summary of workplace expectations, employee benefits, and HR procedures for all regular employees of the enterprise company.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 724 Td
(All employees, contractors, and temporary staff are expected to follow these policies while working on company premises or representing the company externally.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
50 696 Td
(2. Core Workplace Principles) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 678 Td
(Employees must act with integrity, professionalism, respect, and accountability in all business interactions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 660 Td
(Discrimination, harassment, retaliation, and abusive conduct are prohibited across all offices, digital channels, and work-related events.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 642 Td
(Managers are responsible for maintaining inclusive teams and escalating concerns promptly to HR.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
50 614 Td
(3. Employment Standards) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 596 Td
(Standard working hours are 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM, Monday through Friday, unless a role-specific schedule is approved in writing.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 578 Td
(Employees are expected to be punctual, maintain accurate attendance records, and notify their manager before the start of the workday if they are unable to report to work.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 560 Td
(Repeated absenteeism, late arrivals, or failure to follow attendance procedures may result in corrective action.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
50 532 Td
(4. Leave and Time Off) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 514 Td
(Annual leave: 18 paid days per calendar year.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 496 Td
(Sick leave: 10 paid days per calendar year, with medical certification required for absences of three or more consecutive workdays.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 478 Td
(Parental leave, bereavement leave, and unpaid leave may be granted in accordance with local law and company policy.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 460 Td
(Leave requests should be submitted through the HR portal at least five working days in advance when practical.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
50 432 Td
(5. Compensation and Benefits) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 414 Td
(Salary payments are processed monthly and deposited directly into the employee's registered bank account.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 396 Td
(Employees may be eligible for health insurance, retirement contributions, wellness initiatives, and performance bonuses based on role and policy eligibility.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 378 Td
(Questions related to payroll, deductions, or benefit enrollment should be directed to HR Operations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
50 350 Td
(6. Code of Conduct) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
50 332 Td
(Conflicts of interest must be disclosed immediately. Employees may not accept gifts, favors, or payments that could influence business decisions.) Tj
ET
